  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe verifier names a feed plunge that takes more than one stepdown of uncut material in one move (#3679, law (d3)).\n\n- New law `camcraft_sim::verify::plunge_depth`: every non-rapid axial descent is judged against the floor that the cuts before it left under the full tool disc. The take is the move's own bite - the lesser of the move's start and that floor - so a tip that a rapid already stood inside stock answers for its own descent only. A dive from air keeps the full column reading.\n- The gate is `VerifyContext::plunge_stepdown`, the `None` discipline: only the level-cutting kinds state a stepdown (2D Contour, Pocket, Offset2D, Slot, TrochoidalSlot, Adaptive2D, Pocket3D, MultiAxisRough, the staged Face). A tilted 3+2 frame keeps `None`.\n- The finding is advisory by the #3525 pattern: `Warning::PlungeTooDeep { at, mm, limit_mm }`, MCP kind `plunge_too_deep`, UI line 227. The post is not held. The issue's crescent case (an 18 mm plunge beside stock that no level above cut) is named.\n- The program ahead acquits a conviction: `acquit_plunge_by_prior` re-reads each finding against the prior program's surface, the same third term of the min that `acquit_by_prior` gives a rapid. The wiring in `generate.rs` cuts the prior grid when either law convicted.\n- The slack stays the established `z_tol` alone. No wider slack was added: the 0.5 mm overage of the first commit was a floor error and a bite error, not a tolerance error.\n\n## The six reconciled suites\n\nThe first commit (cc1bed29d) over-convicted six pre-existing app tests. All six keep their expected verdicts. No test was changed.\n\n1. `vertical_rapid_stock.rs::a_vertical_rapid_into_a_taller_block_is_named_and_blocks_the_post` - the entry rapid broke the raw top and the feed below it took 2 mm. The bite reading acquits the feed; the rapid conviction stands and holds the post.\n2. `vertical_rapid_stock.rs::a_dive_into_stock_an_earlier_face_removed_posts` - the face left Z 5 standing. The bite reading and the prior acquittal clear the dive.\n3. `carried_stock_entry.rs` (both `assert_safe_entry` failures) - 18 trochoidal microlift plunges of 0.3 mm read the raw 10.5 column; the bite reading acquits them. The one contour plunge read 10.5 where the face had left 10.0, its stepdown exactly; the prior acquittal clears it.\n4. `clearance_in_stock.rs::the_same_plane_over_stock_an_earlier_face_cut_down_holds_only_for_the_first_traverse` - the prior acquittal removes the advisory; the first traverse stands as before.\n5. `top_stock.rs::facing_to_top_removes_the_height_warning_but_a_shallow_face_does_not` - the same face-acquitted dive; the warnings are empty again.\n6. The slack question - the 0.5 mm overage was cured by the honest floor and the honest bite, not by a wider tolerance. The law keeps the established `z_tol`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `camcraft-sim` `plunge_depth` binary: the crescent dive is named (mm 18.0 against the 4.5 stepdown); a dive exactly one stepdown deep, a ring-entry dive in the kerf of the level above, a pecked dive and the `None` gate stay clean; the bite is pinned by `a_feed_that_a_rapid_already_stood_inside_stock_answers_for_its_own_bite_only` and `a_feed_plunge_buried_deeper_than_one_stepdown_is_named_for_its_own_bite`.\n- `camcraft-sim` `verify::prior` units: the plunge acquittal over a cleared pocket, the dive below the prior floor that still stands, the wider tool, the lateral feed, the limit no number can read.\n- `camcraft-app` `plunge_depth_tab`: the catalog case `2d/contour-tabs` names its three tab-window dives (6.0 mm against a 2.0 stepdown), advisory.\n- The six reconciled suites above.\n\n## What was not exercised\n\n- The solids-based re-read of a stepped stock (`acquit_by_stock_top`) is not wired for the feed plunge: a plunge into a casting's low step still reads the raw grid's top. Named under Limits in `docs/decisions/3679-plunge-depth-law.md`.\n- The heavy lanes and the pixel snapshots did not run; the quick gate ran only. The example catalog suites other than the pinned tab case did not run.\n- The tilted 3+2 frames stay unnamed until a pose-aware reading exists.\n\n## Follow-up\n\n- #3722 stays open: decide whether a named over-deep dive stands as a proven floor for the later laws (`Rest::cut` clears its own column).\n\nChangelog: verify names a feed plunge that takes more than one stepdown of uncut material in one move, judged on the move's own bite and acquitted on prior-cut material (advisory `plunge_too_deep`, the post is not held) (#3679)\n\nFixes #3679\n",
